        {
          "resource_id": "monster_action",
          "stats": {
            "action_name": {
              "value": "Constrict"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "Requirements: The clockwork fabricator has a creature grappled or restrained; Effect 2d4+4 bludgeoning, 21 Modular Arms A clockwork fabricator is built to perform a specific type of task repeatedly, and it comes with built-in artisan's tools and two detachable \"arms. \" An adjacent creature can forcibly remove a clockwork fabricator's arm with a successful 18 Thievery check to Disable a Device. A creature can Interact to install a new arm with a successful 18 Engineering Lore check. A fabricator has two of any of the following types of arms.\n\n- Melee 1A buzz-saw blade +16 (forceful, sweep), Damage 1d4+6 slashing plus 1d6 bleed\n- Melee 1A crushing vise +14 (grapple), Damage 2d6+6 bludgeoning plus Grab\n- Melee 1A sledgehammer +12, Damage 2d10+6 bludgeoning\n- Ranged 1A nail gun +11 (agile, range 10 feet), Damage 2d8 piercing\n- Melee 1A pneumatic chisel +14, Damage 2d8+6 piercing\n- Ranged 1A towing anchor +11 (thrown 30 feet), Damage 1d4+6 piercing"
            },
